<!DOCTYPE policyconfig PUBLIC
 "-//freedesktop//DTD PolicyKit Policy Configuration 1.0//EN"
 "http://www.freedesktop.org/software/polkit/policyconfig-1.dtd">

<!-- Lets the three switches in the app do what "sudo secctl" does from a
     terminal.

     allow_active is "yes", and in a security tool that deserves an argument
     rather than a shrug.

     There is nobody to ask. Phosh registers no polkit authentication agent,
     so an action set to auth_admin cannot put a prompt on any screen -
     pkexec fails outright and the switch becomes a control that does
     nothing. The sibling projects hit this before us; modemctl's policy
     carries the same note.

     What it grants is bounded by secctl itself, which is the part that
     matters. The program takes no path, no rule and no sysctl from its
     caller: the three parts are compiled in, the only value that comes from
     outside is a network in CIDR form, and it is rejected unless it parses
     as exactly that. There is no "secctl run", no shell and no way to point
     it at a different file. So the capability handed to the session is
     "turn our own three parts on or off", not "edit /etc as root".

     And the person this is granted to is the person holding the phone, who
     can already reboot it into fastboot. The attacker this whole project is
     about is remote or is unprivileged code in a session - and
     allow_inactive is "no", so an SSH login gets nothing from this. That is
     not a hope: polkit counts an SSH session as inactive, which the sibling
     project verified on this phone with pkcheck against the session process.

     allow_any stays at auth_admin so that anything which is neither of those
     two still has to authenticate. -->

<policyconfig>
  <vendor>misc-de</vendor>
  <vendor_url>https://github.com/misc-de/furios_security</vendor_url>

  <action id="de.misc-de.secctl.manage">
    <description>Change the hardening of this phone</description>
    <description xml:lang="de">Härtung dieses Telefons ändern</description>
    <message>Turning the kernel hardening, the module blocks or the firewall on or off</message>
    <message xml:lang="de">Kernel-Härtung, Modulsperren oder Firewall ein- oder ausschalten</message>
    <defaults>
      <allow_any>auth_admin</allow_any>
      <allow_inactive>no</allow_inactive>
      <allow_active>yes</allow_active>
    </defaults>
    <annotate key="org.freedesktop.policykit.exec.path">/usr/local/bin/secctl</annotate>
    <annotate key="org.freedesktop.policykit.exec.allow_gui">true</annotate>
  </action>
</policyconfig>
